# TASK-260715-2jatnd — M0 packet bridge and HEV decision

- Status: Accepted for the macOS-first prototype scope
- Date: 2026-08-30
- Scope authority: ADR-003, ADR-004, ADR-009, ADR-011, ADR-020, ADR-024
- Decision owner: `TASK-260715-2jatnd`

## Decision

The M0 Bridge gate passes for the active macOS-first prototype scope. The
accepted implementation is the public `NEPacketTunnelFlow` adapter boundary
connected to an `AF_UNIX/SOCK_DGRAM` `PacketFlowBridge`, with unmodified pinned
HEV/lwIP consuming the borrowed endpoint. The decision does not approve SSH,
relay, production routes or DNS, a real Network Extension VPN run on this build
host, iOS, or future performance.

No platform or address-family result is averaged. MTU 8500 fails as the default
candidate because constrained-buffer rows produced 768 `EMSGSIZE` sender
refusals. The physical-iPhone, NAT64, sleep/wake, and whole-extension-memory rows
remain explicitly deferred. ADR-024 makes the physical Apple-silicon Mac the
active M0 target and keeps the iPhone row outside the macOS-first gate; it is
neither a pass nor a waiver.

## Selected initial configuration

| Setting | Selected M0 value | Evidence and rationale |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Provider and HEV MTU | `1500` | Portable baseline. All nominal and mixed IPv4, native IPv6, and dual-stack rows had zero loss. `4096` remains injectable only after end-to-end path proof; `8500` is rejected as the default. |
| Requested bridge send/receive buffers, both socket-pair endpoints | `32768` bytes | The physical matrix measured requested = effective at 4096, 32768, and 262144 bytes. `32768` is the smallest non-fault-injection value; `4096` is pressure-only and values through `262144` remain injectable. Effective values must be read back and a clamp must be reported, never assumed. |
| Work count budget | `64` packets per pump slice | The accepted physical HEV/bridge matrix used 64. Deterministic count-bound tests cover smaller forced yields and count malformed work. |
| Work time budget | `5 ms` per pump slice | The accepted physical HEV/bridge matrix used 5 ms. The bridge uses an injected monotonic clock and yields when either count or time is exhausted. |
| `socks5.udp` | `tcp` | Fixed by ADR-004 and verified against the pinned public HEV configuration surface. |
| `misc.task-stack-size` | `24576` bytes | Effective value remains 24576 only with the selected explicit UDP copy-buffer count. |
| `misc.tcp-buffer-size` | `4096` bytes per session | Accepted low-memory value and unchanged by the pinned HEV clamp. |
| `misc.udp-copy-buffer-nums` | `2` | ADR-020 baseline. Omitting it restores upstream default 10 and silently raises the effective stack to 35480, so omission is invalid. |
| `misc.max-session-count` | `500` initial ceiling | Three producer and three independent reviewer runs passed 100/250/500 stages and intentionally did not force the former 1200 candidate. Raising the ceiling requires new composed memory evidence. |

The 500-session setting supersedes the unmeasured 1200 M0 candidate in the
earlier baseline YAML. It is a configuration ceiling, not proof that teardown
is an instantaneous hard allocation cap. Later physical tuning remains caller
injected and must not mutate these evidence-backed defaults silently.

